  "notes": {
    "ids": "The source of identifiers for new items. It can be unavailable.",
    "store": "Keeps JSON values by key. What it keeps survives a restart.",
    "store.calcs.kept": "Every key with its value, in the order the keys were first put.",
    "store.does.delete": "The key and its value are no longer kept, and the answer is deleted. A key that is not kept is not found, and nothing changes.",
    "store.does.put": "The value (any JSON value, null included) is kept under the key. A key that is already kept keeps its place and gets the new value; a new key goes after the others. A key that was deleted is new when it is put again. Keys are compared exactly, as strings.",
    "todo-api": "The HTTP API of the to-do list. Each request is passed to the list (${Todos}), and the list's answer becomes the response.",
    "todo-api.calcs.get": "The list's items, filtered as asked, are the body, with 200.",
    "todo-api.does.complete": "The item is completed in the list. Completed: 200. Not found: 404. Already done: 409.",
    "todo-api.does.delete": "The item is removed from the list. Removed: 204. Not found: 404.",
    "todo-api.does.post": "The title in the body is added to the list. Created: 201, with the new item. Invalid: 422, with no body. The source of identifiers is unavailable: 503, with no body.",
    "todos": "A to-do list, kept in ${Store}: it survives a restart (after it, it has the same items, in the same order, each open or done as before). Items are added, completed, removed and listed. Each item has an identifier given by the list, a title, and whether it is done.",
    "todos.calcs.listed": "The items in the order they were added: all of them, only the open ones, or only the done ones, as asked.",
    "todos.does.add": "A title that is empty or made only of whitespace, or that has more than 100 characters (a title of exactly 100 is fine), is refused as invalid, with no item. Otherwise a new item with a fresh identifier and the given title, stored exactly as given (not trimmed), goes after the others, and the answer is created, with the item (not done). When no identifier can be had because the source of identifiers is unavailable, a title that is not invalid is refused as unavailable, with no item.",
    "todos.does.complete": "An open item becomes done, and the answer is completed. An item that is already done stays done, and the answer is already-done. An unknown identifier is not found, and nothing changes.",
    "todos.does.remove": "The item is removed, and the answer is removed. An unknown identifier is not found, and nothing changes."
  },
